# Build context exclusions.
#
# `deploy/surfaces/Dockerfile` does `COPY backend /app/backend` and the build
# context is the repository root, so without this file the image would carry
# ~950 MB of backend alone — including `backend/venv`, which is a WINDOWS
# virtualenv and would be both useless and shadowing inside a Linux image.
#
# Nothing excluded here is needed by the surfaces job: the 500 m grid, the LENZ
# raster and the era-offset fields are all fetched from S3 at runtime by
# `entrypoint.sh`, deliberately, because they are gitignored or untracked and
# have never been in a checkout.

# Virtualenvs — the big one, and the wrong platform
venv/
*/venv/
backend/venv/
.venv/

# Python build artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# Large runtime data the job fetches from S3 instead
backend/data/
backend/models/
backend/uploads/
backend/images/

# Elastic Beanstalk's local history of deployment bundles — ~270 MB of old
# zips, and by far the largest thing left in `backend/` once the venv is gone.
.elasticbeanstalk/
backend/.elasticbeanstalk/

# Front ends and their dependencies — no part of this image
packages/
node_modules/

# Repo bulk with no role in the build
.git/
.github/
docs/
alembic/
scratchpad/
*.pdf
*.tif
*.zip
*.jar

# Local environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
